flowchart LR
    accTitle: Samba Active Directory domain controller lab architecture
    accDescr: An administrator and Windows client use an isolated Ubuntu Samba domain controller. The controller provides DNS, Kerberos, LDAP, SYSVOL, NETLOGON, and signed time, forwards non-domain queries to an upstream resolver, synchronizes with external time sources, writes a root-only local online backup, and relies on an operator to move that backup to encrypted offline storage.

    Admin[Administrator<br/>SSH or Windows RSAT]
    Client[Windows lab client]
    DNS[Upstream DNS resolver]
    NTP[External time sources]
    LocalBackup[(Root-only local<br/>online backup)]
    OfflineBackup[(Operator-managed encrypted<br/>offline copy)]

    subgraph LAN[Isolated lab LAN]
        DC[Ubuntu 24.04<br/>Samba AD DC]
        Services[Internal DNS · Kerberos<br/>LDAP · SYSVOL/NETLOGON]
        Chrony[Chrony + Samba<br/>signed-time socket]
        DC --- Services
        DC --- Chrony
    end

    Admin -->|SSH / authenticated administration| DC
    Client -->|DNS, Kerberos, LDAP, SMB| DC
    Chrony -->|signed NTP, LAN only| Client
    DC -->|forward non-AD queries| DNS
    Chrony -->|synchronize host clock| NTP
    DC -.->|archive + checksum| LocalBackup
    LocalBackup -.->|operator copies and encrypts| OfflineBackup
